    "text": "Here's the implementation of the `simplify` function:\n\n```python\ndef simplify(x, n):\n    # Your implementation here\ndef simplify(x, n):\n    # Try to convert the fractions to integers\n    x_val = eval(x)\n    n_val = eval(n)\n    \n    # Calculate the product of the fractions\n    product = x_val * n_val\n    \n    # Check if the product is an integer\n    return product.is_integer()\n    \n# Test cases\nprint(simplify(\"1/5\", \"5/1\"))  # True: True\nprint(simplify(\"1/6\", \"2/1\"))  # False: False\nprint(simplify(\"7/10\", \"10/2\")) # False: False\n```\n\nThis function first converts the input fractions to integers using `eval`, then multiplies them, and checks if the result is an integer. If it is an integer, it returns `True`; otherwise, it returns `False`.",
